From 880345d9bfa230912ca1aa154392236191335617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 21:24:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 178/209] feat(area): component edit mode in Sandbox, proved
 with the box shape

The editor half of scene-notes/area/decisions/02. Three hooks in CEntityObject,
all of them no-ops for an entity whose components do not implement
IEditorShapeComponent, so the legacy path is unchanged:

- GetLocalBounds unions the bounds every such component reports, so framing (F),
  GetBoundBox and rubber-band selection see geometry that owns no entity slot.
  HitTestRect needed no change: it reaches GetLocalBounds through GetBoundBox.
- HitTest gains HitTestEditorShapeComponents, tried after the slot walk and
  before the physics early-out, because a shape volume is real geometry even on
  an entity that also has a physical proxy. The tolerance is the one
  CShapeObject::HitTest uses - screen scale factor plus the hit context's own
  distance tolerance - so an edge stays clickable at any zoom.
- CreateComponentWidget emits one SEditToolButton row per component that names
  an edit tool, labelled by the component. The row resolves the tool by name
  through the class factory, so EditorQt links nothing new, and hands it the
  object and component GUIDs in a SEntityComponentEditToolTarget. Those payloads
  live in a node-based map keyed by component instance, because SetUserData
  takes a bare void* that must outlive a row the inspector rebuilds on every
  selection change.

CShapeEditTool in the editor plugin closes the loop. It is written against
IShapeComponentEdit alone, so it will serve Sphere, Polygon and Spline unchanged;
it draws the hull and screen-constant handles in Display, moves a handle with an
ITransformManipulator, and wraps one gesture in one CUndo - Begin plus StoreUndo
on drag start, Accept on drag end. After each gesture it repeats by hand the
snapshot sandwich the inspector performs during its input pass
(SetOverridePolicy + Read, COMPONENT_PROPERTY_CHANGED, UpdatePrefab), without
which a viewport edit is lost on save, on undo and on game mode. Esc ends the
tool; object and component are re-resolved from GUIDs on every use.

CAreaShapeBoxClassDesc puts "Create Object -> Area -> Box" in the Create panel
from the plugin, reusing EditorQt's CEntityObjectWithComponent machinery through
the class factory rather than subclassing it, which keeps this DLL free of any
link dependency on Sandbox.

